/**
 * AfMath.Variance is a stateless utility service for computing the (population) statistical
 * variance of a collection of numeric values.
 *
 * Contract of {@link AfMath.Variance#variance}: `values` is a required, non-empty array of
 * doubles. The input array is never mutated. The function computes the arithmetic mean of
 * `values`, then returns the mean of the squared deviations from that mean:
 *
 * `variance = (1 / n) * sum((x_i - mean) ^ 2)` for `i` in `0..n-1`
 *
 * This is the *population* variance (divides by `n`), not the sample variance (which would
 * divide by `n - 1`).
 *
 * The array must contain at least one element; calling {@link AfMath.Variance#variance} with an
 * empty array throws an error.
 *
 * Examples:
 * - `variance([1, 2, 3, 4])` -> `1.25` (mean is `2.5`; squared deviations are
 *   `2.25, 0.25, 0.25, 2.25`, whose mean is `1.25`)
 * - `variance([5])` -> `0` (a single value has zero deviation from its own mean)
 * - `variance([2, 2, 2])` -> `0` (all values equal the mean)
 */
service type AfMath.Variance {

  /**
   * Computes the population variance of a non-empty array of doubles.
   *
   * Computes the arithmetic mean of `values`, then returns the arithmetic mean of the squared
   * deviations of each element from that mean (i.e. divides by `n`, not `n - 1`). The original
   * array is not mutated.
   *
   * @param values A required, non-empty array of doubles to compute the variance of.
   * @return The population variance of `values`.
   * @throws if `values` is empty.
   */
  variance: function(values: ![double]): !double js-rhino
}
